  "brief": {
    "asOf": "28 Oct 2026",
    "items": [
      {
        "tab": "payments",
        "tag": "Payments",
        "text": "UPI's September dip is the calendar — daily volume set a record at 802 M. The real story is the 0.4% merchant charge on P2M payments above ₹2,000: announced 15 Sep, survived a stay plea in the Supreme Court, then deferred two days before launch with no new date. Until it returns, UPI's zero-MDR economics stand."
      },
      {
        "tab": "lending",
        "tag": "Lending",
        "text": "The RBI hiked the repo rate 25 bps to 5.50% on 7 Oct — the first hike since Feb'23 — with CPI seen near 5.8% over the next three quarters. Credit still grew 19.4%, but deposits at 17.8% have nearly closed the gap that defined 2026. Expect loan growth to cool in H2."
      },
      {
        "tab": "wealthtech",
        "tag": "Wealth",
        "text": "SIPs hit another record at ₹32,490 cr while industry AUM fell 5.1% — quarter-end debt redemptions of about ₹1.83 L cr, not retail flight. Groww holds 29% of NSE active clients; Angel One is 36k clients short of overtaking Zerodha for second."
      }
    ]
  },
